# Job 13 (not in the first list): LTO alone for libunit in an external app.
# Job 11 cannot separate LTO from -O2 for libunit, because the cc -O2 of the
# lab_capp link (remote.sh:156) lifts the fat libunit.a objects to -O2 in B.
# Here both sides have libunit.a at -O2: A is master 856d23b9e plus
# patches/cflags-o2.diff, B adds LTO with patches/cflags-o2-lto-fat.diff. The
# difference between the sides is LTO only (unitd, libnxt.a and libunit).
# How the patch is applied, the lab image and the reasons for the empty FUNCS
# and for STRACE=0 are in the header of job 07.
# PRIMARY is s_instructions, as in job 11.
JOB=13-o2-lto-capp
REV_A=856d23b9ed2cecbd96d5452cf790f828fc55d700
REV_B=856d23b9ed2cecbd96d5452cf790f828fc55d700
PATCH_A=patches/cflags-o2.diff
PATCH_B=patches/cflags-o2-lto-fat.diff
WORKLOAD=capp
CONNS=6
WARM=2
DUR=8
REPS=4
PERF=1
PRIMARY=s_instructions
EXPECT=s_instructions lower in B by more than the null band (guess before any run: 0 to 3 percent); r_instructions lower as in job 09; ok equal, bad 0, alerts 0
FALSIFY=s_instructions NO CLAIM or NOISY, or higher in B: LTO for libunit gives nothing this lab can resolve once both sides are at -O2
